   "subject": "Re: Is exist any item appropriateness measure in the mixedmirt() context?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I would think that Rhat (also known as PSR) is only a &quot;convergence statistic&quot; of the MCMC chain. It is not intended as a kind of item appropriateness statistic (a.k.a . item fit statistic).<br><br>Alexander</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Am Sonntag, 12. März 2017 14:42:04 UTC+1 schrieb Phil Chalmers:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I think that Rhat value is strictly a fully MCMC estimation statistic, though I&#39;m sure Alexander could explain what it is better than I.</div><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Phil</span><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sun, Mar 12, 2017 at 7:52 AM, Seongho Bae <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">seongh...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I meant, is exist any &#39;Rhat&#39; values internally in mixedmirt() class products like sirt::<a href=\"http://mcmc.2pno.ml\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mcmc.2pno.ml&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474652134000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3UQ0hr9O8Keka3kdTR7-C9\">mcmc.2pno.ml</a>. <div><br></div><div>Seongho<br><div><br>2017년 3월 11일 토요일 오전 5시 2분 54초 UTC+9, Phil Chalmers 님의 말:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><div dir=\"ltr\">Sorry, I don&#39;t follow what you are asking here.</div></span><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Phil</span><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><span>On Thu, Mar 9, 2017 at 1:34 AM, Seongho Bae <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">seongh...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></span><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><div dir=\"l